attribution: The tune "Slane" is a traditional Irish air first printed in Patrick W. Joyce's Old Irish Folk Music and Songs (1909). The words are Eleanor Hull's 1912 verse setting (she died in 1935) of Mary Byrne's 1905 translation (she died in 1931) of an early Irish poem. Melody and words are public domain worldwide.
